# Zoo ↔ Cursor Sync

Edit skills/rules/mandates in **either** location. Sync runs automatically.

## Where to add things

| Add in Cursor | Also appears in Zoo |
|---------------|---------------------|
| `.cursor/skills/zoo-my-skill/SKILL.md` | `.roo/skills/{bucket}/my-skill/SKILL.md` |
| `.cursor/rules/zoo-my-mandate.mdc` | `.roo/rules/cursor-export/my-mandate.md` |

| Add in Zoo | Also appears in Cursor |
|------------|------------------------|
| `.roo/skills/{bucket}/my-skill/SKILL.md` | `.cursor/skills/zoo-my-skill/` |
| `.roo/rules/NN-my-mandate.md` | `.cursor/rules/zoo-my-mandate.mdc` |

**Conflict rule:** newest file wins per pair.

## Automation

- **On Cursor session start** → full sync
- **After agent edits** to `.cursor/skills/`, `.cursor/rules/zoo-*`, `.roo/skills/`, `.roo/rules/` → debounced sync
- **Manual:** `node scripts/sync-zoo-cursor.mjs`
- **Log:** `.cursor/zoo-sync.log`

## New skill in Cursor only

Create `.cursor/skills/zoo-{name}/SKILL.md` → sync creates `.roo/skills/engineering/{name}/` (bucket inferred from name).

## New mandate in Cursor only

Create `.cursor/rules/zoo-{name}.mdc` with `alwaysApply: true` → sync exports to `.roo/rules/cursor-export/{name}.md`.

Restart Cursor after first hook setup so `hooks.json` loads.
